	(text "EE22/08/13 (PC95) 2-LAYER REVERSIBLE-STACK 1:1 PLANAR TRANSFORMER — REV 1.0\nONE SINGLE 2-LAYER PCB DESIGN -> STACK 2 IDENTICAL BOARDS PER TRANSFORMER (ZERO JUMPER WIRES):\n  1. Board 1 (Bottom, F.Cu UP = PRIMARY): Solder Pins 1 & 2 (Trans_in1, Trans_in2); Pins 3 & 4 pass through 1.80mm NPTH.\n  2. Insulation Barrier: Place 0.10mm Kapton tape sheet across Board 1 copper winding (>4 kV Pri-Sec isolation).\n  3. Board 2 (Top, Flip 180 deg in Y, B.Cu UP = SECONDARY): Solder Pins 3 & 4 (Trans_A, Trans_B); Pins 1 & 2 pass through NPTH.\n  4. Core: Assemble 1x pair EE22/08/13 (PC95) through the 3 milled cutouts (6.30x14.50 center, 2x 4.30x14.50 outer).\nStackup: 2-Layer 0.80mm FR-4, 1oz (35um) Cu on F.Cu & B.Cu | Winding: 12T CW (6T+6T, 420um W / 220um G, 0.365mm slot clr).\nElectrical Spec (1:1, 12T:12T, Lm=720uH nom): Drive Trans_in1/in2 with bipolar +/-12V H-bridge (150-250 kHz)\n  through 10uF 25V X7R DC-block + 4.7 ohm 0.25W damper -> V_rect = 11.75V DC -> V_GS = 11.05V (81.2% 3-ch eff, 1.82A inrush).\nMates to mosfet_gate_driver (a00c78f) J14/J15/J16 (1x4, 2.54mm): Pin1=Trans_in1(Dot), Pin2=Trans_in2, Pin3=Trans_A(Dot), Pin4=Trans_B."
		(exclude_from_sim no)
		(at 53.34 116.84 0)
		(effects (font (size 1.45 1.45)) (justify left top))
		(uuid "06a58716-2213-538e-835a-be48d68f4d78")
	)
